 "notes": "Headline solar dark photon limit: red solid line in Fig.1 left panel (2020solar.pdf in the e-print), the new XENON1T S2-only constraint at 90% C.L. on kinetic mixing epsilon vs dark photon mass m_V, for the hard Stueckelberg mass case (solid). This supersedes the older XENON10 (blue/purple) solid curve. Extracted from vector PDF via pymupdf get_drawings: red stroke color (1,0,0), dashes=[]; axes calibrated from major tick strokes (x: 51.5px->1e-3 eV, 37.08px/decade; y: 249.29px->1e-14... using 44.5px/decade with 249.29px=1e-15). Boundary built as lower envelope in mass, RDP-downsampled in log-log. epsilon is the kinetic mixing chi (reported directly, not squared). Curve spans ~0.015 eV (rises to plot top 1e-10) through valley min eps~1.1e-14 near 200-240 eV, up to steep high-mass cutoff ~540 eV. Solar-emission limit: independent of local DM density (dm_density_assumed=null). The paper also reports a dark-photon-dark-matter limit (Fig.1 right, black lines) but the solar limit is the leading headline result. Dashed red Higgsed (e prime=0.1) curve not used.",
